The final content_shell link fails with:

    undefined reference to `base::debug::ReadProcMaps(std::string*)'
    undefined reference to `base::debug::ParseProcMaps(std::string const&,
        std::vector<base::debug::MappedMemoryRegion, ...>*)'

The HaikuPorts patchset drops base/debug/proc_maps_linux.cc for Haiku, which
is right -- it parses /proc/self/maps and Haiku has no /proc -- but unlike
every other file it removes there (process_handle, process_metrics,
platform_thread, sys_info, file_path_watcher all gain a Haiku or stub
replacement) it supplies nothing in its place. base/debug/stack_trace_posix.cc
still compiles its SandboxSymbolizeHelper, because USE_SYMBOLIZE is on for
this build, and calls both entry points.

Add the replacement alongside the other Haiku sources. The file itself is
vendored at chromium87_overlay/upstream/missing_sources/base/debug/
proc_maps_haiku.cc; both stubs report "no maps", which every caller already
handles by symbolizing without them.

--- a/chromium/base/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chromium/base/BUILD.gn
@@ -2013,6 +2013,7 @@
       "process/process_handle_haiku.cc",
       "process/process_iterator_haiku.cc",
       "process/process_metrics_haiku.cc",
+      "debug/proc_maps_haiku.cc",
       "threading/platform_thread_haiku.cc",
       "system/sys_info_haiku.cc"
     ]
